    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.8</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:24:32 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22308</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Chats open at the newest message every time, never on a blank screen.</li><li>Your message and Working… appear the moment you send; the approval card sits right above the composer.</li><li>A chat only says finished when it really is: while helpers run it says Waiting for N background tasks.</li><li>Skip approvals takes effect at once, even for a request already waiting.</li><li>Typing while the agent works steers it instead of restarting it.</li><li>Tighter, Conductor-like spacing; thinking folds into one line.</li><li>Errors read as plain sentences with Retry, never internal error.</li><li>Three shared presets (Best, Balanced, Save usage) set which Claude model plans, codes and runs commands; pick one when you start a thread and edit them in Settings.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.7</h4><ul><li>Dropdowns, including the model picker, stay attached to their controls when their contents update instead of opening far away.</li><li>The web app has clearer dashboard and phone navigation, easier access to usage, and pond logos in place of decorative color dots.</li><li>A new thread opens straight into its chat instead of saying Squeak no longer lists it.</li><li>Threads started from a pond keep their workspace, so they no longer vanish from the sidebar; ones that did come back.</li><li>Fixes Squeak running hot and freezing while a chat is open: the running timer and the chat layout no longer redraw the whole conversation many times a second.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.6</h4><ul><li>Squeak cloud now lives in Settings › Account. If this Mac isn't connected yet, press Connect… there; Settings › Cloud is gone.</li><li>Fixes Settings saying you were signed in while still asking you to sign in.</li><li>Model names read the same everywhere, like Opus 5.5 · 1M and GPT 6.1 Sol, instead of raw ids.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
